# document_claims.p0t — SC2-A: frase, claim e commitment restano separati.
#
# Fonti vere e parafrasi corte:
# - Salmonella simulation study:
#   https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/
# - NASA DART technical report:
#   https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804
#
# Le tre formule epistemiche entrano parlando come membri di classi naturali.
# Il C non contiene quelle formule e il retract deve cambiare anche claim gia'
# osservate senza cancellare superficie, fonte o attribuzione.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test long units survive and multiword markers are teachable]
!timeout 60
# Il primo periodo supera la profondita' che SC1 materializzava: deve restare
# intero anche se non possiede ancora uno status.
> read: The investigators predict that higher initial Salmonella counts increase the likelihood of septic shock and death. The model outputs show that outcomes were highly correlated with initial Salmonella counts.
< Learned 0 fact(s), skipped 2.
!query document_unit(document_1, document_1_unit_0, 0)
!query document_unit_token_surface(document_1_unit_0, 16, death)
!query document_unit(document_1, document_1_unit_1, 1)
!query! current_document_typed_claim(document_1_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)

# La menzione quotata conserva la locuzione esatta attraverso learn/query/retract.
> "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker.
< Learned: hypothesis_report_marker("the investigators predict that").
> Is "the investigators predict that" a hypothesis report marker?
< Yes.
> forget that "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker
< I no longer treat «"the investigators predict that"» as a hypothesis report marker.
> Is "the investigators predict that" a hypothesis report marker?
< No.
!query! hypothesis_report_marker(forget)

[test source addressed claims status and ablation]
!timeout 60
> "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker.
< Learned: hypothesis_report_marker("the investigators predict that").
> "the measurements indicate that" is an observation report marker.
< Learned: observation_report_marker("the measurements indicate that").
> "the model outputs show that" is a simulation result marker.
< Learned: simulation_result_marker("the model outputs show that").

# REPLAY: una ipotesi attribuita e un risultato simulato non diventano fatti
# del mondo. URI + fingerprint generano lo stesso document id fra processi.
> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/ The investigators predict that high infection increases mortality. The model outputs show that outcomes correlate with initial infection.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_53e12a4bf22efa6c)
!query claim_status(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query! claim_status(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, observed)
!query claim_status(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_1_claim_0, simulated)
!query claim_attributed_to(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, document_authors)
!query claim_commitment(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, attributed_only)
!query holds_in(context(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0), proposition(surface("high infection increases mortality")))

# TRANSFER sperimentale: status opposti nello stesso documento e nessuna
# promozione della frase ipotizzata a commitment del mondo.
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The investigators predict that kinetic impact can alter an asteroid orbit. The measurements indicate that DART shortened the orbital period of Dimorphos.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_ed942df7bdb84575)
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_1_claim_0, observed)
!query! holds_in(world, proposition(surface("kinetic impact can alter an asteroid orbit")))

# TRANSFER osservazionale: il risultato riportato resta distinto dalla
# conclusione causale ipotizzata, sotto una fonte open-access diversa.
> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5118066/ The investigators predict that observational associations can misrepresent causal effects. The measurements indicate that some observational associations differed from randomized effects.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5118066/")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_be8b48c1dd3343bc)
!query claim_status(document_5c0b5aed1874ec5b_be8b48c1dd3343bc_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_status(document_5c0b5aed1874ec5b_be8b48c1dd3343bc_unit_1_claim_0, observed)
!query! claim_status(document_5c0b5aed1874ec5b_be8b48c1dd3343bc_unit_0_claim_0, observed)

# TRANSFER di simulazione climatica: `simulated` non collassa in `observed`.
> read: https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/ The investigators predict that high resolution improves predictive skill. The model outputs show that high resolution improved precipitation forecasts.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_cb48b8510480033c)
!query claim_status(document_60abb92fbf13d97b_cb48b8510480033c_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_status(document_60abb92fbf13d97b_cb48b8510480033c_unit_1_claim_0, simulated)
!query! claim_status(document_60abb92fbf13d97b_cb48b8510480033c_unit_1_claim_0, observed)

# ABLATION: lo status e il context dipendente spariscono dal documento vecchio;
# proposition, fonte e attribuzione restano. Il risultato osservato non dipende
# dalla classe ritratta e rimane vivo.
> forget that "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker
< I no longer treat «"the investigators predict that"» as a hypothesis report marker.
!query! claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query document_claim(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575, document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, proposition(surface("kinetic impact can alter an asteroid orbit")))
!query claim_attributed_to(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, document_authors)
!query claim_source_span(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0, range(32, 42))
!query! claim_commitment(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, attributed_only)
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_1_claim_0, observed)

# RETEACH riattiva la vista sul documento gia' osservato, senza rileggerlo.
> "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker.
< Learned: hypothesis_report_marker("the investigators predict that").
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_commitment(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, attributed_only)

# ── SC2-B — LA NORMALIZZAZIONE E' UNA FASE PURA E CONTESTUALE ────────────────
#
# SC2-A conservava chi ha riportato che cosa, con quale status, dove e sotto
# quale fonte; il «che cosa» restava una stringa. Qui il remainder attraversa la
# STESSA analisi con cui parrot0 legge una frase detta in chat — nessun parser
# documentale parallelo — ma il candidato che ne esce non entra nel mondo.
#
# Le locuzioni e i verbi di questo blocco sono HELD-OUT rispetto alla KB
# persistita: entrano parlando dentro il test. Se una baseline comincia a
# passare senza la sua lezione, la crescita della KB ha reso verde il proprio
# cricchetto: si sostituiscono i membri, non si abbassa l'attesa.
#
# Fonti vere:
#   NASA DART            https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804
#   GMD WRF ad alta ris. https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/
#   PMC ricerca osserv.  https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5118066/
#   PMC Salmonella ABM   https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test sc2b baseline: senza marker non esiste ne' la claim ne' la domanda]
!timeout 60
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The investigators predict that a kinetic impactor deflected an asteroid. The measurements indicate that DART slowed the orbital period.
< Learned 0 fact(s), skipped 2.
!query! document_claim($D, $C, $P)
> what did the measurements indicate?
<! reports it as

[test sc2b il marker apre la claim, il contenuto resta superficie]
!timeout 90
> "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker.
< Learned: hypothesis_report_marker("the investigators predict that").
> "the measurements indicate that" is an observation report marker.
< Learned: observation_report_marker("the measurements indicate that").
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The investigators predict that a kinetic impactor deflected an asteroid. The measurements indicate that DART slowed the orbital period.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
# Nessun verbo di relazione noto: la claim resta intera e il fallimento e'
# tipato, non silenzioso.
!query claim_normalization_gap(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, no_reading)
!query! claim_normalized(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, reported)
# La domanda di contenuto risponde gia' dalla superficie, con status e fonte.
# La forma interrogativa non e' stata insegnata: e' la locuzione del marker
# senza il complementatore.
> what did the measurements indicate?
< The source reports it as observed: DART slowed the orbital period (from https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804).
> what did the investigators predict?
< The source reports it as hypothesized: a kinetic impactor deflected an asteroid (from https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804).

[test sc2b la lezione normalizza il remainder e non lo committa mai]
!timeout 90
> slowed is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(slowed).
> deflected is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(deflected).
# REPLAY del turno che prima lasciava un gap.
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The investigators predict that a kinetic impactor deflected an asteroid. The measurements indicate that DART slowed the orbital period.
<~ 2 proposition(s) normalized in quarantine
!query claim_frame(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, slowed, dart, orbital_period)
!query claim_frame(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_0_claim_0, deflected, kinetic_impactor, asteroid)
!query claim_normalized(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, reported)
# LA PROVA CHE CONTA: normalizzare non e' credere.
!query! slowed(dart, orbital_period)
!query! deflected(kinetic_impactor, asteroid)
!query! holds_in(world, proposition(frame(slowed, roles(subject(dart), object(orbital_period)))))
!query holds_in(context(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0), proposition(frame(slowed, roles(subject(dart), object(orbital_period)))))
!query claim_commitment(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, attributed_only)
# E la risposta ha una prova che risale a documento, fonte, unita', span e cue viva.
!query claim_proof(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, proof(document(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab, "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804"), unit(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1), span($R), cue(observation_report_marker, $Cue)))

[test sc2b la verifica di status passa dalla stessa fase pura]
!timeout 60
> was it observed that DART slowed the orbital period?
< Yes - that claim is reported as observed (from https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804).
# CONTRASTO: la stessa proposizione sotto lo status sbagliato non diventa un si'.
> was it hypothesized that DART slowed the orbital period?
< No - that claim is reported as observed, not hypothesized.
> was it simulated that a kinetic impactor deflected an asteroid?
< No - that claim is reported as hypothesized, not simulated.
# PARAFRASI: stessa locuzione, altro ordine interrogativo.
> the investigators predict what?
< The source reports it as hypothesized: a kinetic impactor deflected an asteroid (from https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804).

[test sc2b transfer su tre fonti reali mai usate per progettare la lezione]
!timeout 120
> "the model outputs show that" is a simulation result marker.
< Learned: simulation_result_marker("the model outputs show that").
> raised is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(raised).
> weakened is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(weakened).
> increased is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(increased).

> read: https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/ The investigators predict that higher resolution raised forecast skill. The model outputs show that higher resolution raised precipitation skill.
<~ 2 proposition(s) normalized in quarantine
!query claim_frame(document_60abb92fbf13d97b_aafd7a95b852090a_unit_1_claim_0, raised, higher_resolution, precipitation_skill)
!query! raised(higher_resolution, precipitation_skill)
> what did the model outputs show?
< The source reports it as simulated: higher resolution raised precipitation skill (from https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/).
> was it simulated that higher resolution raised precipitation skill?
< Yes - that claim is reported as simulated (from https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/).
> was it observed that higher resolution raised precipitation skill?
< No - that claim is reported as simulated, not observed.

> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5118066/ The investigators predict that confounding weakened observational evidence. The measurements indicate that randomization weakened confounding.
<~ 2 proposition(s) normalized in quarantine
!query claim_frame(document_5c0b5aed1874ec5b_4812de2cea9b84f5_unit_0_claim_0, weakened, confounding, observational_evidence)
!query! weakened(confounding, observational_evidence)
> was it observed that randomization weakened confounding?
< Yes - that claim is reported as observed (from https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5118066/).

> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/ The investigators predict that a higher initial load increased mortality. The model outputs show that a higher initial load increased septic shock.
<~ 2 proposition(s) normalized in quarantine
!query claim_frame(document_0c04338180aa7436_cb1980b6655fa30b_unit_0_claim_0, increased, higher_initial_load, mortality)
!query! increased(higher_initial_load, mortality)
> what did the investigators predict?
< The source reports it as hypothesized: a higher initial load increased mortality (from https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/).

[test sc2b una lettura parziale e' un gap, non una normalizzazione]
!timeout 90
# «the orbital period OF DIMORPHOS» si legherebbe a slowed(dart, orbital_period)
# e perderebbe di CHI sia il periodo. Una verifica costruita su meta'
# proposizione confonderebbe due claim diverse: la policy di copertura la
# rifiuta, e la claim di superficie resta intera.
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The measurements indicate that DART slowed the orbital period of Dimorphos.
<~ Mapped 1 document unit(s), 1 reported claim(s), and 1 live epistemic status(es)
!query claim_normalization_gap(document_0246e706600fd069_c3be613435057657_unit_0_claim_0, partial_reading)
!query! claim_normalized(document_0246e706600fd069_c3be613435057657_unit_0_claim_0, reported)
!query document_claim(document_0246e706600fd069_c3be613435057657, document_0246e706600fd069_c3be613435057657_unit_0_claim_0, proposition(surface("DART slowed the orbital period of Dimorphos")))
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_c3be613435057657_unit_0_claim_0, observed)
> what did the measurements indicate?
< The source reports it as observed: DART slowed the orbital period of Dimorphos (from https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804).
# E la verifica non inventa un si' su una proposizione che non sa normalizzare.
> was it observed that DART slowed the orbital period of Dimorphos?
<! Yes -
# Una coordinazione lascia fuori il secondo predicato: stesso gap, stessa onesta'.
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The measurements indicate that DART slowed the period and raised the plume.
<~ Mapped 1 document unit(s), 1 reported claim(s), and 1 live epistemic status(es)
!query claim_normalization_gap(document_0246e706600fd069_828cb8ddc2347273_unit_0_claim_0, partial_reading)
!query! claim_normalized(document_0246e706600fd069_828cb8ddc2347273_unit_0_claim_0, reported)

[test sc2b ablation: cade lo strato epistemico, resta la proposizione]
!timeout 90
> forget that "the measurements indicate that" is an observation report marker
< I no longer treat «"the measurements indicate that"» as a observation report marker.
!query! claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, observed)
!query! claim_commitment(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, attributed_only)
!query! holds_in(context(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0), proposition(frame(slowed, roles(subject(dart), object(orbital_period)))))
# La proposizione normalizzata e la superficie sopravvivono al retract: il
# livello debole non muore quando cade quello forte.
!query claim_frame(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, slowed, dart, orbital_period)
!query claim_surface(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, "DART slowed the orbital period")
!query claim_attributed_to(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, document_data)
# E la domanda torna onestamente a non essere capita, invece di rispondere da
# una memoria che non ha piu' giustificazione.
> what did the measurements indicate?
<! reports it as
> was it observed that DART slowed the orbital period?
<! Yes -
# La classe non ritratta resta viva su ogni documento gia' letto. La domanda di
# contenuto e' invece limitata al documento CORRENTE, che qui e' l'ultimo letto:
# e' un limite dichiarato, non un difetto nascosto.
!query claim_status(document_0c04338180aa7436_cb1980b6655fa30b_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_marker_live(document_0c04338180aa7436_cb1980b6655fa30b_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesis_report_marker)

[test sc2b reteach e retention]
!timeout 90
> "the measurements indicate that" is an observation report marker.
< Learned: observation_report_marker("the measurements indicate that").
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0, observed)
!query holds_in(context(document_0246e706600fd069_017fecedd77de3ab_unit_1_claim_0), proposition(frame(slowed, roles(subject(dart), object(orbital_period)))))
